The pikchr R package wraps Pikchr
=================================

The pikchr R package is an R interface to Pikchr (https://pikchr.org), the
PIC-like diagram language created by D. Richard Hipp, the author of SQLite.
The language, its parser and its SVG renderer are his work. Pikchr is modelled
on PIC, the picture language created by Brian W. Kernighan.

The R package is an independent wrapper. It is not affiliated with, maintained
by or endorsed by the Pikchr or SQLite projects or their author.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pikchr (bundled as src/pikchr.c)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

src/pikchr.c is the pikchr.c file distributed by the Pikchr project (generated
there by the Lemon parser generator from pikchr.y), with small changes for use
from R: an R entry point, R's error and print routines in place of exit() and
fprintf(stderr, ...). The upstream check-in is recorded in the MANIFEST_*
macros at the top of the file.

